# =============================================================================
# .gitignore - Custom Traveler Engine
# =============================================================================
# The project lives INSIDE the game folder, so this file works as a WHITELIST:
# everything in the root is ignored (game files, MelonLoader, Unity data, logs,
# Mods/ output, tree.txt...) and only what is listed in section 2 is tracked.
#
# NEVER commit game files or anything under MelonLoader/ (it contains the
# game's decompiled code).
# =============================================================================

# 1) Ignore everything in the repo root
/*

# 2) ...except the project itself
!/.gitignore
!/README.md
!/LICENSE
!/build.bat
!/buildScrap.bat
!/CustomTravelerEngine/
!/TravelerScraper/
!/examples/

# 3) Inside the tracked folders: build output and IDE files
bin/
obj/
.vs/
.vscode/
.idea/
*.user
*.suo
*.pdb
*.cache

# 4) Safety net: binaries and generated files never go in the repo
#    (upload the compiled DLLs as GitHub Release assets instead)
*.dll
*.exe
*.zip
*.log
ct.conf

# 5) OS junk
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
.DS_Store
